// Title: EvilNum APT Golden Chickens Deployment Via OCX Files
// Sigma ID: 8acf3cfa-1e8c-4099-83de-a0c4038e18f0
// Status: test | Level: critical
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2020-07-10 | Modified: 2023-03-09
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218.011
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects Golden Chickens deployment method as used by Evilnum and described in ESET July 2020
//   report
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.welivesecurity.com/2020/07/09/more-evil-deep-look-evilnum-toolset/
//   - https://app.any.run/tasks/33d37fdf-158d-4930-aa68-813e1d5eb8ba/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-emerging-threats/2020/TA/Evilnum/proc_creation_win_apt_evilnum_jul20.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "regsvr32" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/s" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/i" and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\AppData\\Roaming\\" and ProcessCommandLine contains ".ocx"
